not limited to: treatment procedures, drawing blood, performing EKGs, administrat... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / ATHLETICS EQUIPMENT OPERATIONS Athletics - Internal Operations Professional & Administrative -Salary External 09/17/2026 Develops, manages and facilities all policies and procedures that relate to football equipment operations in the Athletics Department. Manages an equipment budget for annual purchases including uniforms, helmets, headsets, practice equipment, sideline apparel and other equipment operational needs. Responsible for safety awareness, precautions and compliance as it relates to practice and game da... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / PROFESSIONAL LEARNING PROGRAM College of Education & Human Services Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Center for Excellence in STEM Education (CESE) Assistant Director of Professional Learning Program provides support in professional learning experiences, research, grant writing and publications within the College of Education and Human Services’ Center for Excellence in STEM Education. View Details Bookmark AUDITOR / SENIOR AUDITOR Internal Audit Professional & Administrative -Salary External Reporting to the Director of Internal Audit, this position plans, performs, and documents risk-based operational, financial, information technology, and compliance audits and other projects independently to evaluate university governance, risk management, and control processes. This position performs all phases of audits/investigations including conducting an audit risk assessment, conducting a... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR - RECRUITMENT / COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences Professional & Administrative -Salary External Under the supervision of the dean, the coordinator of recruiting is responsible for planning, coordinating, and staffing the College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences (CLASS) recruiting events and for building strong working relationships across the University to grow CLASS enrollment. The coordinator serves as the college’s primary liaison to CMU Admissions and works closely with Academic ... View Details Bookmark DIRECTOR/ASSESSMENT & EVALUATION Charter Schools for Gov John Engler Center Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is responsible for leading The Center for Charter School’s functions associated with the analysis and use of data, evaluation of the performance of authorized schools, and oversight of school assessment practices. The Director of Assessment & Evaluation (DAE) ensures that relevant staff have the information they need to make decisions regarding academic school performance and ... View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE CMU Online Professional & Administrative -Salary External The associate director of marketing operations for CMU Online is an operations-focused role responsible for driving the organization, coordination, and execution of integrated marketing efforts that support online and adult learners. This position manages the development and delivery of full-funnel marketing content across digital (web, social, email) and print channels, ensuring work moves eff... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / DESIGN & VISUAL MEDIA CMU Online Professional & Administrative -Salary External The assistant director of design and visual media for CMU Online is a design-focused role responsible for creating and delivering high-quality visual and multimedia assets that support integrated marketing efforts for online and adult learners. This position produces audience-centered creative across digital channels (web, social, email, and video) and print materials (brochures, flyers, and re... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR/COMMUNICATION & ED OUTREACH Gov John Engler Center for Charter Schools Professional & Administrative -Salary External Supports the Center with communications, social media efforts, and the production of marketing materials that advance the Center’s initiatives. Supports outreach efforts through the facilitation of programming for high school students. View Details Bookmark APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III Applications & Systems - OIT Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Application Administrator supports the administration, maintenance, security, and continuous improvement of enterprise applications and related systems used across Central Michigan University. Working as part of a collaborative team, this position helps ensure these services are reliable, secure, and effective for the faculty, staff, and students who depend on them. The role includes techni... View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / FINANCIAL PLANNING & BUDGETS Financial Planning & Budgets Professional & Administrative -Salary External Responsible for financial planning and budgetary matters that arise in the absence of the university budget officer/assistant to the president for strategic planning (UBO) and supports a wide range of financial planning and budget-related matters. This position plays a lead role in budgetary support for the campus community and manages collaborative working relationships and relevant oversight ... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / CEREMONIES & EVENTS President's Office Professional & Administrative -Salary External Reporting to the chief of staff to the president, the ceremonies and events coordinator is responsible for the development, management, oversight, execution, and assessment of all events led by the Office of the President. The coordinator works collaboratively with stakeholders across and external to the university to execute event planning and logistics. This position also maintains the Office... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / RISK MANAGEMENT, ENVIRONMENTAL HEALTH & SAFETY Risk Management, Environmental Health & Safety Professional & Administrative -Salary External Under general supervision, develops, i