    "https://www.consumer.ftc.gov/articles/0243-job-scams": {
      "title": "Job Scams",
      "description": "Job Scams | Consumer Advice Skip to main content An official website of the United States government Here’s how you know Here's how you know The .gov means it’s official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you’re on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. Español CFG: Secondary Menu Report Fraud Read Consumer Alerts Get Consumer Alerts Visit ftc.gov Menu CFG: Main Menu Mega Show/hide Shopping and Donating menu items Shopping and Donating Make smart shopping decisions, know your rights, and solve problems when you shop or donate to charity. View Shopping and Donating Video Topics Topics Shopping For the Home Health Funerals Buying and Owning a Car Donating to Charity Consumer Alerts Scammers are spoofing car dealership websites: What you need to know September 1, 2026 BCP Staff While the car-buying process can be stressful, whether you’re shopping online or in person, the thought of driving off the dealer’s lot with that sweet ride you’ve had your eyes on can be exhilarating. But imagine showing up at the dealership and finding out the dealer has no record of your order or your payment. And that there’s no shiny car waiting for you! That’s what’s happening to unwitting car buyers who’ve been duped by scammers impersonating a car dealership. View all Consumer Alerts Get Consumer Alerts Show/hide Credit, Loans, and Debt menu items Credit, Loans, and Debt Learn about getting and using credit, borrowing money, and managing debt. View Credit, Loans, and Debt Video Topics Topics Credit and Debt Loans and Mortgages Consumer Alerts Struggling with tax debt? Here’s what to know August 13, 2026 BCP Staff If you owe back taxes, there are ways to get real help. But dishonest companies will promise to get rid of your debt for “pennies on the dollar,” before even looking into your tax situation. They’ll often charge service fees without actually doing anything for you, and leave you further in the hole with local, state, or federal tax authorities. View all Consumer Alerts Get Consumer Alerts Show/hide Jobs and Making Money menu items Jobs and Making Money What to know when you're looking for a job or more education, or considering a money-making opportunity or investment. View Jobs and Making Money Video Topics Topics Money-Making Opportunities and Investments Jobs Education and Training Consumer Alerts Are ads on social media vetted or checked for scams? Here’s what to know August 10, 2026 BCP Staff You’re browsing your social media feed when an ad grabs your attention mid-swipe: that designer bag you’ve been dreaming of is 50% off for a limited time only! You’re dying to get your hands on one, so you don’t think twice about clicking on the ad. Why would you? The ad is right there in your feed and it looks real, so you trust that it’s legit. But it might not be. That’s because social media platforms don’t always thoroughly vet the ads you see or the advertisers behind them. View all Consumer Alerts Get Consumer Alerts Show/hide Unwanted Calls, Emails, and Texts menu items Unwanted Calls, Emails, and Texts What to do about unwanted calls, emails, and text messages that can be annoying, might be illegal, and are probably scams. View Unwanted Calls, Emails, and Texts Video Topics Topics Unwanted Calls Unwanted Emails, Texts, and Mail Consumer Alerts Ignore calls, texts, and emails threatening to arrest you for missing jury duty June 11, 2026 BCP Staff Did you get a call claiming you missed jury duty and need to pay? Followed by a text or email with official-looking documents saying there’s a warrant out for your arrest? As alarming as these things sound, they’re a scam designed to steal your money. View all Consumer Alerts Get Consumer Alerts Show/hide Identity Theft and Online Security menu items Identity Theft and Online Security How to protect your personal information and privacy, stay safe online, and help your kids do the same. View Identity Theft and Online Security Video Topics Topics Identity Theft Online Privacy and Security Protecting Kids Online Consumer Alerts See a QR code parked somewhere? Don’t scan it…yet! September 3, 2026 BCP Staff Ever tried to pay for parking and discovered you need to scan a QR code to pay? It seems like a convenient way to pay, but it turns out scammers like using QR codes, too. People have reported scammers covering up legit QR codes on parking meters with a QR code of their own. If you scan that scammy QR code, it could take you to a fake site designed to steal your money, your personal information, or both. So, how can you protect yourself from these scams? View all Consumer Alerts Get Consumer Alerts Scams Search Show/hide Search menu items Items per page 20 50 100 Filters Fulltext search Español CFG: Secondary Menu Report Fraud Read Consumer Alerts Get Consumer Alerts Visit ftc.gov CFG: Main Navigation Shopping and Donating Show/hide Shopping and Donating menu items Shopping For the Home Health Funerals Buying and Owning a Car Donating to Charity Credit, Loans, and Debt Show/hide Credit, Loans, and Debt menu items Credit and Debt Loans and Mortgages Jobs and Making Money Show/hide Jobs and Making Money menu items Money-Making Opportunities and Investments Jobs Education and Training Unwanted Calls, Emails, and Texts Show/hide Unwanted Calls, Emails, and Texts menu items Unwanted Calls Unwanted Emails, Texts, and Mail Identity Theft and Online Security Show/hide Identity Theft and Online Security menu items Identity Theft Online Privacy and Security Protecting Kids Online Scams Show/hide Scams menu items Gift Card Scams Government and Business Impersonators Phone Scams Romance Scams Scams Against Immigrants Scams Against Older Adults Scams Against Small Businesses Wire Transfer Scams Items per page 20 50 100 Filters Fulltext search Breadcrumb Home Articles Vea esta página en español Article Job Scams Scammers advertise jobs the same way honest employers do — online (in ads, on job sites, and social media), in newspapers, and sometimes on TV and radio. They promise you a job, but what they want is your money and your personal information. Here are some examples of jobs scams and advice on how to avoid them . Examples of Job Scams How To Avoid a Job Scam Advice on Finding a Job What To Do If You Paid a Scammer Report Job Scams to the FTC Looking for a business opportunity? Before you get into any money-making program, read Multi-Level Marketing Businesses and Pyramid Schemes and When a Business Offer or Coaching Program Is a Scam to make sure you’re not getting into a bogus business opportunity or a scam. Examples of Job Scams Work-from-home job scams Many people would like to make money working from home. Scammers know this, so they place ads, often online, claiming that they have jobs where you can make thousands of dollars a month working from home with little time and effort. The job could be anything from reshipping products to selling things to people you know . Sometimes the scammers try to get you interested by saying that you can be your own boss , start your own business, or set your own schedule. But instead of making money, you end up paying for starter kits, so-called training, or certifications that are useless. You might also find that your credit card is charged without your permission, or you get caught up in a fake check scam , where you deposit a check from your new employer, the employer then asks you to send some money back due to “overpayment,” but the check will ultimately bounce, and the bank will want you to repay the full amount of the fake check, while the scammers keep the real money you sent them. If someone offers you a job and claims that you can make a lot of money in a short period of time with little work, that’s almost certainly a scam. Here are some examples of work-from-home job scams: Reshipping scams . If you’re searching for a job online, you might see positions advertised for quality control managers or virtual personal assistants that have been placed by scammers. But here’s how you can tell it’s a reshipping scam: once you’re “hired,” the company says that your “job” is to receive packages at home, throw away the original packaging and receipts, repackage the products, and then reship them to an address they give you. Sometimes the address is overseas. The products are often high-priced goods, like name-brand electronics, bought using stolen credit cards. Reshipping goods is never a real job. That’s simply being part of a scam. Sometimes the company tells you it will send your first paycheck after you work for a month, but the paycheck never arrives. And when you try to contact the company, you’ll find that the phone number is often no longer connected and the website is deactivated. This “job” is a scam, and if you gave your personal information thinking it was for payroll, you may now have an identity theft problem. Reselling merchandise scams . In this scam, you may get a call out of the blue from a stranger offering you a job opportunity. Or you may see an ad online or in your local newspaper. They say you can make money buying brand-name luxury products for less than retail prices, and resell those products for a profit. But after you pay for the products, the package never arrives or, if it does, it’s usually junk. Nanny, caregiver, and virtual personal assistant job scams Scammers post fake job ads for nannies, caregivers , and virtual assistants on job sites. Or they may send emails that look like they’re from someone in your community. The message might also seem to come from someone who is part of an organization you know, like your college or university. If you apply, the person who hires you might send you a check. They’ll tell you to deposit the check, keep part of the money for your services, and send the rest to someone else. That’s a scam. A legitimate employer will never ask you to do that. The check is fake and will bounce, and the bank will want you to repay the full amount of the fake check, while the scammer keeps the real money you sent them. So: if you get an offer that includes depositing a check and then using some of the money for any reason, that’s a scam. Walk away. Mystery shopper scams Getting paid to shop sounds like a dream job — especially if you’re going to school full-time or looking for a side job. But while some mystery shopping jobs are honest, many are scams. Honest mystery shopping companies won’t ask you to pay for certifications, directories of jobs, or job guarantees. If someone asks you to pay to get a job, that’s a scam. And if they want you to deposit a check and send money back, stop. That’s a sign of a fake check scam. Read Mystery Shopping Scams to learn more. Job placement service scams While many staffing agencies, temporary agencies, headhunters, and other placement firms may deliver honest job search services, others lie about what they will do for you, promote outdated or fake job openings, and charge fees for so-called services. Honest placement firms do not typically charge a fee to job candidates. Instead, the hiring company pays them a fee to find qualified candidates. If a placement firm asks you for a fee — especially one you have to pay in advance — walk away. You’re probably dealing with a scam. Government and postal jobs scams Information about job openings with the federal government or U.S. Postal Service is free and available to everyone. And it’s always free to apply for a federal or postal job. Never respond to an ad that promises jobs with the federal government or postal service. And don’t pay a fee to get the job. Those are scams. Use official government websites to find and apply for a job with the federal government at USAJobs.gov , or visit usps.com/employment to find jobs with the U.S. Postal Service. How To Avoid a Job Scam Before you accept a job offer, take these steps to avoid common job scams: Search online. Look up the name of the company or the person who’s hiring you, plus the words “scam,” “review,” or “complaint.” See if others say they’ve been scammed by that company or person. No complaints? It doesn’t guarantee that a company is honest, but complaints can tip you off to possible problems. Talk to someone you trust . Describe the offer to them. What do they think? This also helps give you vital time to think about the offer. Don't pay for the promise of a job . Honest employers, including the federal government, will never ask you to pay to get a job. Anyone who does is a scammer. Never bank on a “cleared” check. No honest potential employer will ever send you a check to deposit and then tell you to send on part of the money, or buy gift cards with it. That’s a fake check scam . The check will bounce, and the bank will want you to repay the amount of the fake check. Advice on Finding a Job When you’re searching for a job, start with safe and reliable sources: USAJobs.gov — This is the federal government’s official site with job openings nationwide. CareerOneStop — Sponsored by the U.S. Department of Labor, CareerOneStop lists hundreds of thousands of jobs. It also links to employment and training programs in each state. USA.gov — Find local government websites, which list any open positions they may have on their websites. Also, when you’re applying for a job, an employer may do a background check. Read Employer Background Checks and Your Rights to learn more. What To Do if You Paid a Scammer No matter how you paid — debit or credit card , mobile payment app or wire transfer , gift card , cash reload card, or cryptocurrency — immediately contact the company you used to send the money, report the fraud, and ask to have the transaction reversed, if possible. For specific advice on how to reverse different types of payments, read What To Do If You Were Scammed . Report Job Scams to the FTC If you see a job scam, or lose money to one, report it to the FTC at ReportFraud.ftc.gov . You can also report it to your state attorney general . Find out more about how to avoid scams at ftc.gov/scams . Search Terms job search jobs scam Topics Jobs and Making Money Jobs Scams All Scams Job Scams March 2023 Related Items What To Do if You Were Scammed Return to top Menu CFG: Footer Menu Feature Pages Articles Consumer Alerts Videos CFG: Footer Menu Right Report Fraud Get Consumer Alerts CFG: Footer ftc.gov About Us Contact Us Privacy and Notices FOIA Office of Inspector General"
    },
    "http://med.cmich.edu/cmepcareers": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | CMU Health Skip to main content MyChart Appointments Call Chat sign in SEARCH About Services Find a Doctor Patients Locations Careers Back to CMU Home Search About Services Find a Doctor Patients Locations Careers MYCHART Appointments Call Chat Back to Main Menu In This Section Related Links In This Section Related Links In This Section Related Links In This Section Related Links In This Section Related Links In This Section Related Links Careers Teach. Treat. Discover. Lead. Great Lakes Bay Region Careers CMU Health career opportunities Take the next step in your career with CMU Health! CMU Medical Education Partners, a non-profit medical education corporation that has over 50 years of experience delivering medical education to students and residents, has successfully partnered with area hospitals and CMU College of Medicine , to provide superior academic programs, exceptional patient experiences and rewarding careers. At CMU Health, it is our mission to combine compassion with extraordinary medical care for our patients every day. Here, you have the opportunity to teach, treat and lead positive change to improve health throughout the region. We are a constantly growing team of faculty physicians, licensed care providers and support team members. VIEW STAFF AND PHYSICIAN CAREER OPPORTUNITIES Why choose CMU Health? Friendly, caring faculty, resident and employee culture. Largest multi-specialty practice in the Great Lakes Bay Region. Opportunity to teach, treat and lead change and improve regional health. Clinic located in a heath care hub, featuring ambulatory and hospital settings. Community sees 52,000 clinic patient visits annually. Medium-sized city within a friendly community. Low cost of living and ample housing with an easy commute. Vibrant local attractions and outdoor activities for a high quality of life. IN THIS SECTION Careers Great Lakes Bay Region CMU Careers return to top of page Locations Saginaw 1000 Houghton Ave. Saginaw, MI 48602 989-746-7500 Driving Directions Mount Pleasant 600 East Preston St. (Foust Hall 200) Mount Pleasant, MI 48859 989-774-6599 Driving Directions SEE ALL LOCATIONS CMU HEALTH About Leadership Locations Insurance & Fees Prescriptions RESOURCES Find a Doctor MyChart Careers News & Media Web Store SERVICES Primary Care Behavioral Medicine Surgery Women's Health & OB/GYN Mount Pleasant Clinics PARTNERSHIPS Partnerships Great Lakes Bay Region Mental Health Initiative Centering Programs CMU Medical Education Partners Nondiscrimination Statement Privacy Policy Website Accessibility Website Feedback Consumer Information Campus Safety Information and Resources © Copyright Central Michigan University | Mount Pleasant, MI 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000"
    },
    "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "Central Michigan University: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:www.jobs.cmich.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs Central Michigan University: All Jobs 2026-08-17T14:22:21-04:00 https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45328 2026-08-17T14:22:20-04:00 2026-08-17T14:22:21-04:00 UNIVERSITY CENTER FACILITY OPERATIONS WORKER <div>The UC Facility Operations Worker plays a key role in event set up and maintaining cleanliness in the University Center (UC) by performing custodial, operations, and facility management tasks.</div> University Center https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45423 2026-09-04T00:00:21-04:00 2026-09-04T00:00:22-04:00 COORDINATOR - STANDARDIZED PATIENT SIMULATION CENTER / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE <div>This position assists with coordination and supervision of the daily events and activities of the Standardized Patient-Simulation Center, on and off campus. This position will assist internal and external clientele to fulfill the needs of the program and plan future events. Responsibilities include assessing and managing problems on and off-site, monitoring quality assurance of events, promoting relationships, creating assignments, and assisting in the supervision of student workers. The Coordinator orients and organizes learners participating at program events and activities. This position is also responsible for facilitating Standardized Patient (SP) sessions and mutual communication among administration personnel, SP’s, clients, and the public. This position assists in the recruitment, screening, selection, training, and evaluation of SP’s. Extreme flexibility and superb interpersonal skill are required for cultivating relationships with participants, so that they will be willing to respond to the needs of the program in a variety of situations.</div> Medicine, College of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44830 2026-05-13T09:50:18-04:00 2026-05-13T09:50:19-04:00 Bachelor of Science in Nursing Lecturer <div>The Nursing Program at Central Michigan University invites applications for a full-time fixed-term faculty position beginning in August 2026 for the Fall 2026 semester. The successful candidate will provide instructional leadership in maternity and pediatric nursing, including didactic teaching and oversight of clinical instructors assigned to related clinical courses. The faculty member will also teach other nursing courses as assigned based on program needs. Other teaching-related activities of this position may include student advising and satisfying accreditation or professional standards, where applicable.<br><br>This position requires collaboration with faculty, staff, and clinical instructors to support student success, course quality, and program effectiveness. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to course coordination, curriculum implementation, and ongoing program development.</div> Rehab and Medical Sciences, School of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45390 2026-08-28T16:43:33-04:00 2026-08-28T16:43:33-04:00 ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE <div>The associate director of marketing operations for CMU Online is an operations-focused role responsible for driving the organization, coordination, and execution of integrated marketing efforts that support online and adult learners. This position manages the development and delivery of full-funnel marketing content across digital (web, social, email) and print channels, ensuring work moves efficiently from concept through to completion. While contributing to content direction and writing as needed, the primary focus is maintaining momentum by keeping projects on track, aligning stakeholders, and ensuring timely execution. Working in close collaboration with CMU Online’s marketing director, the associate director plays a key role in coordinating campaigns, managing timelines, and ensuring marketing efforts are delivered effectively, aligned with audience needs, and supportive of CMU Online’s enrollment goals.</div> Innovation & Online https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45342 2026-08-19T12:29:03-04:00 2026-08-19T12:29:04-04:00 TEMPORARY MASON (PART-TIME) <div>Performs skilled work in the construction, repair and maintenance of masonry structures; performs related work as required.</div> Facilities Management https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45396 2026-08-31T15:09:28-04:00 2026-08-31T15:09:29-04:00 DIRECTOR/ASSESSMENT & EVALUATION <div>This position is responsible for leading The Center for Charter School’s functions associated with the analysis and use of data, evaluation of the performance of authorized schools, and oversight of school assessment practices. The Director of Assessment &amp; Evaluation (DAE) ensures that relevant staff have the information they need to make decisions regarding academic school performance and contractual performance. The DAE works with other Center staff in providing ongoing assessment of the Center’s academic accountability metrics and makes recommendations for changes as necessary. The DAE also ensures the Center’s partner schools are utilizing the most current practices in academic assessment. The DAE is responsible for ensuring the Center is well positioned to advance its efforts by using data to inform authorizing practices, advance policy and to target resources effectively. The DAE also has oversight responsibility for contractual assessment practices of all partner schools. The DAE also is responsible for training Center staff in the communication, implementation, and interpretation of assessment best practices and accountability standards to ensure valid and reliable results are collected on academic assessments used for informative and evaluative purposes.</div> Gov John Engler Center for Charter Schls https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44934 2026-06-09T12:23:09-04:00 2026-06-09T12:23:10-04:00 PROJECT ADVISOR / UPWARD BOUND (2 POSITIONS) <div>This position is located in Detroit, Michigan and serves students within a Detroit Public Schools Community District High School and Charter Schools. The Project Advisor position is a federally-funded TRIO program providing opportunities for participants to succeed in their precollege performance and ultimately in their higher education pursuits. The Project Advisor assists in planning, implementing and administering the goals and objectives of the TRIO Upward Bound program. This job requires a level of independence to respond to requests from the Project Director, university personnel, school administrators, community partners, students, and parents within defined grant regulations, guidelines, and procedures.</div> TRIO Programs - Detroit https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45349 2026-08-20T08:51:13-04:00 2026-08-20T08:51:13-04:00 COORDINATOR / RISK MANAGEMENT, ENVIRONMENTAL HEALTH & SAFETY <div>Under general supervision, develops, implements and maintains environmental, health and safety programs in support of the University's mission and in compliance with university policies, procedures, state and federal regulations and standards to ensure the environmental health and safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Works in coordination with campus community while providing guidance and consultation to university personnel regarding hazardous waste/hazardous material response, industrial hygiene, indoor air quality, environmental compliance and other related activities.</div> Risk Mgmt, Environmental Health & Safety https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/42259 2025-01-30T10:00:30-05:00 2025-01-30T10:00:30-05:00 BOOKSTORE TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Temporary bookstore positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary bookstore positions available. Charges CMU Bookstore customers for their purchases using credit and debit cards, student accounts, checks and cash using a point-of-sale (POS) register. Helps students find their books, re-shelves books, and straightens shelves. Buys back books at the end of the semesters.</div> CMU Bookstore https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45398 2026-09-01T00:00:36-04:00 2026-09-01T00:00:42-04:00 SUPERVISOR / ARCHITECTURAL TRADES <div>Supervises and coordinates activities of employees in the architectural trades, including but not limited to carpentry, painting, locksmith, and masonry trades in the maintenance and renovation of campus facilities. This position also oversees projects related to commercial roofing installation and repair. Must have the ability to be on-call and able to respond to emergency situations in a timely manner.</div> Architectural Trades https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45176 2026-07-21T10:55:34-04:00 2026-07-21T10:55:35-04:00 ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / ALTERNATIVE BREAKS <div>The Assistant Director of the Mary Ellen Brandell Volunteer Center (VC) will work collaboratively with the Director and other professional staff and student members of the Volunteer Center to develop, support, and promote service opportunities to engage students with the mission and values of Central Michigan University. The Assistant Director will serve as the university advisor to the Alternative Breaks (AB) program and provide oversight and direction to the VC and AB graduate and undergraduate student staff. The Assistant Director will direct leadership training of the Alternative Break student advisory board, the student site leaders, and provide oversight of participant development of 700 students. The Assistant Director will also be responsible for providing support to Volunteer Center and AB program assessment. Additionally, the Assistant Director will manage most of the marketing efforts of the office, including, but not limited to: designing and printing promotional materials, promotional items ordering, social media posting for all channels, weekly newsletter creation and distribution and management of the Engage Central volunteer database. The Assistant Director will supervise up to three students to assist with the office’s marketing and social media efforts. The Assistant Director will provide oversight of the AB budget and scholarship development as well as board and site leader retreats, service development with university community partners, and develop recruitment strategies for the program.</div> Volunteer Ctr https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45359 2026-08-21T15:13:47-04:00 2026-08-21T15:13:48-04:00 COORDINATOR / CEREMONIES & EVENTS <div>Reporting to the chief of staff to the president, the ceremonies and events coordinator is responsible for the development, management, oversight, execution, and assessment of all events led by the Office of the President. The coordinator works collaboratively with stakeholders across and external to the university to execute event planning and logistics. This position also maintains the Office of the President and Board of Trustees web presence, assists with searches for senior officer positions that report directly to the president, and assists with other special projects.</div> President's Office https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/42262 2025-01-30T10:00:38-05:00 2025-01-30T10:00:39-05:00 MALE UROGENITAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (MUTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>In-house training for males to teach, assess, and provide feedback to learners about accurate urogenital and rectal examination techniques. The MUTA addresses the communication skills needed to provide a comfortable exam in a standardized manner, while using their body as a teaching tool in a supportive, non-threatening environment. The MUTA teaches the proper technique for performing the urogenital exam, including external and internal inspection and palpation. Urological exam procedures to include palpation for lymph nodes, hernias, and examination of the scrotum, testicles, penis, and rectum (Prostate). The MUTA guides the student through the learning process while each learner performs the urologic exam on the MUTA's body.</div> Medicine, College of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45407 2026-09-01T13:42:19-04:00 2026-09-01T13:42:20-04:00 ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II/PT <div>Works in a team environment to schedule appointments and perform all check-in processes accurately and appropriately for all CMU Health Services patients (multiple clinics, multiple providers). Enters medical insurance and demographic information into the electronic medical record. Collects copays and past due balances. Performs daily reconciliation and reporting of payments. Stays current on basic health insurance specifics, guidelines, and rules. Maintains the confidentiality, security, and organization of CMU Health Services medical records. Releases patient information as appropriate following HIPAA and FERPA guidelines. Performs a variety of basic office duties.</div> University Health Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45216 2026-07-28T14:08:02-04:00 2026-07-28T14:08:02-04:00 CUSTODIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Temporary custodian positions. No benefits. A custodian is the key University and Facilities Management person in maintaining cleanliness of academic, residential, and administrative campus buildings and service areas. Performs manual custodial tasks in care of University buildings; performs related work as required.</div> Facilities Management https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45364 2026-08-24T12:54:22-04:00 2026-08-24T12:54:23-04:00 ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II <div>This position is responsible for providing administrative support to the Office of Environmental Health &amp; Safety/Emergency Management a part of the Risk Management, Environmental Health &amp; Safety unit. The person in this position must be able to work at a high degree of independence while supporting multiple staff members including coordinating meetings, developing and distributing meeting minutes and maintaining budgetary records. In addition this position is responsible for monitoring and providing updates to the department internet web pages and general office duties.</div> Risk Mgmt, Environmental Health & Safety https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/42300 2025-02-04T09:02:41-05:00 2025-02-04T09:02:41-05:00 CHP STANDARDIZED PATIENT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Standardized patient simulation involves the use of individuals trained to portray the roles of patients, family members or others to allow students the opportunity to develop, practice and enhance their interviewing skills, communication skills, physical exam/evaluations, and history taking techniques. Students participate in multiple standardized patient exercises throughout their healthcare education.<br><br>Using a creative and innovative approach, a Standardized Patient (SP) is a person carefully recruited and vigorously trained on assigned cases to take on the characteristics of a real patient thereby affording the student an opportunity to learn and to be evaluated on clinical skills in a simulated clinical environment.<br><br>The IPEP Center has an ongoing process of hiring and training a diverse and comprehensive group of Standardized Patients, encompassing all ages, races, ethnic groups, religions, genders, etc. They will be classified as a temporary employee and will not receive any additional benefits associated with the University.<br><br>Working as a Standardized Patient (SP) provides a unique opportunity to be involved in shaping the medical education of tomorrow’s health professionals.</div> The HH & GA Dow College of Health Prof https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45410 2026-09-01T16:08:17-04:00 2026-09-01T16:08:18-04:00 AUDITOR / SENIOR AUDITOR <div>Reporting to the Director of Internal Audit, this position plans, performs, and documents risk-based operational, financial, information technology, and compliance audits and other projects independently to evaluate university governance, risk management, and control processes. This position performs all phases of audits/investigations including conducting an audit risk assessment, conducting audit research, preparing the audit programs, evaluating risks and controls, testing control effectiveness to ensure compliance (with regulations, laws, policies, procedures), documenting audit work papers, drafting audit reports (including findings and recommendations), and presenting findings to auditee and management. Work assigned to the Auditor is expected to be carried out with an appropriate and reasonable amount of supervision. The Auditor should be proactive in initiating audit steps and checking with the supervisor when clarity is needed. Work assigned to the Senior Auditor is expected to be carried out with minimal supervision.</div> Internal Audit https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45245 2026-07-31T10:13:34-04:00 2026-07-31T10:13:35-04:00 PHYSICS/MACHINE SHOP TECHNICIAN II <div>Responsible for setting up and disassembling instructional laboratories, repairs and maintains laboratory equipment, controls departmental supply and equipment inventory, uses machine and wood shop techniques to fabricate and/or modify instructional and research equipment.</div> Physics https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44229 2026-01-09T17:15:17-05:00 2026-01-09T17:15:17-05:00 X-ray Studies of Quantum Materials Postdoctoral Research Fellow <div>A postdoctoral position is available starting February 1, 2026, in the Physics Department at Central Michigan University. We are seeking an enthusiastic scientist to work in the field of structural characterization of quantum materials using x-ray scattering techniques and structure modeling.</div> Physics https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45370 2026-08-25T08:57:07-04:00 2026-08-25T08:57:08-04:00 MEDICAL SUPPORT STAFF POOL (RN, CMA, RMA, LPN) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Under the supervision of full-time medical staff, individuals in this role support the daily operations of the Student Health Services Clinic or Primary Specialty Clinic. Responsibilities are determined by the licensure and qualifications of the individual and include direct patient care and administrative support. The clinic provides a broad range of services, including routine medical care, physicals, chronic disease management, allergy injections, immunizations, birth control management, full-service laboratory testing, STI screening and treatment, and travel health consultations. Team members are expected to contribute to the delivery of high-quality, patient-centered care in a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment.</div> University Health Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45414 2026-09-03T08:19:03-04:00 2026-09-03T08:19:04-04:00 ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / PROFESSIONAL LEARNING PROGRAM <div>The Center for Excellence in STEM Education (CESE) Assistant Director of Professional Learning Program provides support in professional learning experiences, research, grant writing and publications within the College of Education and Human Services’ Center for Excellence in STEM Education.</div> Education & Human Svcs, College of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45261 2026-08-04T15:03:24-04:00 2026-08-04T15:03:24-04:00 JOURNEYMAN CARPENTER (2 POSITIONS) <div>Performs skilled work in the construction, maintenance and repair of structures, equipment and articles of wood; performs related work as required.</div> Carpentry Shop https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44305 2026-01-27T11:02:24-05:00 2026-01-27T11:02:25-05:00 ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Part-time temporary administrative office assistant positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary administrative office assistant positions available in various departments. Duties and responsibilities vary by department but are primarily focused on providing secretarial support for specific departments. Responsibilities may include scheduling meetings, answering the phone, drafting correspondence and maintaining records.</div> HR - Employment Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45373 2026-08-25T11:49:45-04:00 2026-08-25T11:49:45-04:00 ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT/CMU ONLINE <div>The Associate Vice President (AVP) has oversight of the academic unit within the CMU Online Learning enterprise. In partnership with academic colleges, departments, and university stakeholders, the AVP supports the development, delivery, and growth of online, hybrid, and off-campus academic and professional learning opportunities. The AVP collaborates with faculty and academic leadership to advance credit and noncredit programming, including undergraduate, graduate, certificate, micro-credential, and professional development offerings. The position also oversees prior learning initiatives, competency-based education efforts, and select interdisciplinary programs administered through CMU Online. The AVP is responsible for growing the number of academic and noncredit programs delivered online and at distance, working with outreach teams to grow customized learning solutions, dual enrollment, and community college partnerships, and expanding and developing alternative routes to credit through prior learning, competency based, and other progressive approaches. Reporting to the vice president of CMU Online, the AVP advances innovative, accessible, and student-centered learning opportunities aligned with the university’s strategic priorities.</div> HR - Employment Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45417 2026-09-03T11:27:26-04:00 2026-09-03T11:27:27-04:00 CLINICAL RESEARCH NURSE / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE <div>This position is comprised of both clinical and regulatory responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include assisting with developing and implementing the activities of a clinical research trial which consists of pre-screening patients for study eligibility and performing delegated study tasks including but not limited to: treatment procedures, drawing blood, performing EKGs, administration and accountability of study medication/study devices, recording adverse events, monitoring patient retention, withdrawals, ethical/legal practices, and audit preparation. This position may be expected to act as the primary contact with the sponsor's study monitoring individual(s), be a resource for developing operational plans, become an expert regarding the study plan, and maintain awareness of all ongoing activities, ensuring proper handling of all paperwork. Depending upon the type and complexity of a given trial, these roles and responsibilities may be shared with or assigned to other research staff at the discretion of the director of clinical research or principal investigator (PI). Regulatory responsibilities include understanding compliance with federal, state, and local laws as they relate to the performance of human patient's research, as well as preparation and maintenance of all regulatory documentation for assigned studies. This position may be responsible for presenting the study to the Institutional Review Board (IRB) and/or other departments. It is the responsibility of the position to schedule and conduct study specific training for any additional staff within the research department as well as ancillary departments. Travel may be required between clinical sites for training or study related patient visits mainly throughout the Saginaw/Tri-Cities area.</div> Medicine, College of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45281 2026-08-06T16:24:27-04:00 2026-08-06T16:24:27-04:00 MANAGER/LIBRARY SYSTEMS <div>Provides strategic leadership, coordination, and operational expertise for University Libraries’ systems in a collaborative, service oriented environment. This 12 month, non tenure track librarian position is responsible for the planning, implementation, oversight, and continued evolution of library systems across their full lifecycle, ensuring reliable services that align with library and university priorities. This position serves as a key advisor to library leaders on systems strategy, budget recommendations, and emerging technologies, while also performing hands on configuration, maintenance, and problem solving for core library platforms. The position is the primary connector among library units, library technology vendors, and campus partners, translating library technology needs, constraints, and opportunities into actionable solutions and supporting library services, staff workflows, and user needs. Supervises the Coordinator of Marketing and Branding.</div> Libraries - Library Systems https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44324 2026-01-28T17:00:29-05:00 2026-01-28T17:00:30-05:00 ACADEMIC TUTOR/FACILITATOR TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Provides academic assistance to students in all academic areas and workshop facilitation as needed. Tutors work with TRIO Detroit Upward Bound and Educational Talent Search programs in Southwest and Northwest, Detroit within our target schools.</div> TRIO Programs - Detroit https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45384 2026-08-27T10:43:10-04:00 2026-08-27T10:43:11-04:00 APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III <div>The Application Administrator supports the administration, maintenance, security, and continuous improvement of enterprise applications and related systems used across Central Michigan University. Working as part of a collaborative team, this position helps ensure these services are reliable, secure, and effective for the faculty, staff, and students who depend on them. The role includes technical support, system configuration, monitoring, documentation, troubleshooting, and participation in planning and improvement efforts that advance the Office of Information Technology’s goals, service standards, and commitment to excellent customer support.</div> Applications & Systems - OIT https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45318 2026-08-14T00:00:20-04:00 2026-08-14T00:00:21-04:00 COORDINATOR / TEACHER & SPECIAL EDUCATION PREPARATION PATHWAYS <div>The teacher and special education preparation pathways coordinator works in the Department of Teacher and Special Education at Central Michigan University and supports multiple educator preparation pathway programs. This position provides leadership and coordination for program operations, candidate advising, recruitment, reporting, clinical placement processes, and accreditation-related activities. Working closely with the department chairperson, program directors, faculty, the Office of Educator Preparation, and PK-12 partners, the coordinator promotes candidate success while ensuring effective program implementation and compliance with university, state, and accreditation require</div> Teacher & Special Education https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45421 2026-09-03T16:23:06-04:00 2026-09-03T16:23:06-04:00 ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT III <div>-Primary support person for department, including MA in Economics Graduate Program -Primarily responsible for day-to-day office operations, including supervision of student assistants -Primarily responsible for maintaining and analyzing budgetary records, including ProfEd off-campus and online tuition and expenses, faculty grants and professional development accounts -Primarily responsible for purchasing and maintaining equipment. -Primarily responsible for scheduling paperwork including assignment of classrooms.</div> Economics https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44740 2026-04-15T17:25:10-04:00 2026-04-15T17:25:11-04:00 VICE PRES/RESEARCH & SPONSORED PROGRAMS <div>Central Michigan University (CMU) is classified as a Carnegie Research 2 (R2): High Research Spending and Doctorate Production institution, with high research activity and doctoral education. The Vice President for Research and Sponsored Programs (VPRSP) reports to the Provost/Executive Vice President and provides senior leadership across the university to develop and implement a clear vision for advancing and strengthening CMU's research enterprise. As a senior member of the university’s leadership team, the VPRSP advises institutional leadership on research strategy, policy, investment, and risk, and represents CMU internally and externally on matters related to research, scholarship, creative work, and innovation.<br><br>The VPRSP cultivates a strong culture of scholarship, creative work, research, development, and innovation; advances institutionally aligned, interdisciplinary, and community-engaged research initiatives; expands strategic research initiatives and partnerships; and further develops the university’s infrastructure and administrative support for research and compliance in ways that enable institutional growth.<br><br>The VPRSP provides leadership for the Office of Research and Sponsored Programs, which includes Research Compliance, Laboratory and Field Safety, and Animal Facilities (vivaria), and encompasses functions pertaining to sponsored programs, partnerships, intellectual property and technology transfer, human subjects research, biosafety, and export control. The VPRSP ensures these functions operate in a coordinated and efficient manner that supports responsible growth in research activity.</div> HR - Employment Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45387 2026-08-28T10:13:09-04:00 2026-08-28T10:13:10-04:00 ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / DESIGN & VISUAL MEDIA <div>The assistant director of design and visual media for CMU Online is a design-focused role responsible for creating and delivering high-quality visual and multimedia assets that support integrated marketing efforts for online and adult learners. This position produces audience-centered creative across digital channels (web, social, email, and video) and print materials (brochures, flyers, and recruitment collateral), ensuring consistent, engaging design execution across all platforms. In close collaboration with CMU Online’s director of marketing, this role leads the visual expression of the unit’s campaigns, maintaining brand cohesion and elevating the effectiveness of marketing initiatives through strong, strategic design.</div> Innovation & Online https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45336 2026-08-19T09:05:41-04:00 2026-08-19T09:05:42-04:00 INSTALL REPAIR TECH I/II - OIT <div>Responsible for installation, removal, rearrangement and maintenance on a variety of complex communication and security equipment. May repair and/or add to the University's switch and database.</div> Telecommunication Services-OIT https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45426 2026-09-04T16:54:19-04:00 2026-09-04T16:54:20-04:00 ASSOCIATE ATHLETIC TRAINER <div>The Associate Athletic Trainer is a certified and licensed healthcare professional responsible for delivering comprehensive athletic training services to Central Michigan University (CMU) intercollegiate student-athletes. This position plays an integral role within the Sports Medicine team and reports to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine.</div> Athletics - Sports Medicine https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45394 2026-08-31T08:19:25-04:00 2026-08-31T08:19:26-04:00 Assistant Women's Basketball Coach <div>Duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to, assisting with organization and administration of the women’s basketball program including practice and game coaching, recruiting, scouting, social media and public relations.</div> Athletics https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44897 2026-06-02T00:01:14-04:00 2026-06-02T00:01:16-04:00 INDUSTRIAL HYGIENIST TEMPORARY <div>Temporary position. No benefits. Assists the Director of the Office of Laboratory and Field Safety with implementing various lab safety programs on campus. Works in coordination with campus community while providing laboratory safety services (chemical, biological, radiological, and laser).</div> Laboratory & Field Safety https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45348 2026-08-20T00:01:24-04:00 2026-08-20T00:01:26-04:00 DIRECTOR / ACADEMIC & PROFESSIONAL PROGRAMS <div>The director of academic and professional programs within the CMU Online department provides administrative oversite for undergraduate interdisciplinary academic degree programs and certificates, delivered online and at distance. The director is responsible for leading the effort to craft a strategic vision for prior learning credit initiatives, facilitating communication between main campus, faculty, staff, and those involved with the delivery of programs via CMU Online. The director also provides updates to the curriculum, reviews policies and procedures, seeks new opportunities for expansion, and optimizes effectiveness. The director oversees the academic operations of degrees and certificates including admissions, curriculum development, interdisciplinary council, collaborations among campus departments, student learning outcomes assessment, program review, resolution of student issues, and faculty approvals.</div> Academic and Professional Programs https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45397 2026-09-01T00:00:36-04:00 2026-09-01T00:00:38-04:00 COORDINATOR - RECRUITMENT / COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES <div>Under the supervision of the dean, the coordinator of recruiting is responsible for planning, coordinating, and staffing the College of Liberal Arts &amp; Social Sciences (CLASS) recruiting events and for building strong working relationships across the University to grow CLASS enrollment. The coordinator serves as the college's primary liaison to CMU Admissions and works closely with Academic Advising, Success Coaches, CMU Online, CMU Athletics, and other campus units to align, coordinate, and schedule recruitment initiatives that connect prospective and current students to CLASS programs. The coordinator partners closely with CLASS chairs and programs to stay current with their programs and students. The coordinator works closely with the CLASS Hub to recruit students by leveraging Hub services.</div> Liberal Arts & Social Sci, College of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45165 2026-07-17T14:33:36-04:00 2026-07-17T14:33:36-04:00 Synthesis and Chemical Biology of Mycobacterial Glycolipids Postdoctoral Research Fellow <div>One postdoctoral research fellow position focused on the synthesis and chemical biology of mycobacterial glycolipids is available starting September 1, 2026, in the laboratory of Dr. Ben Swarts in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Central Michigan University. The initial appointment for this position is one year, with the expectation of renewal, contingent upon funding and satisfactory performance. <br><br>We are looking for an enthusiastic chemist to work on the synthesis, characterization, and chemical biology of structurally complex, virulence-associated glycolipids from the cell envelope of mycobacterial pathogens, such as <em>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em>. We are seeking talented individuals with demonstrated experience in the chemical synthesis and chemical biology of complex carbohydrates, lipids, and conjugates thereof. Candidates should have strong written and oral communication skills with a track record of publication and presentation of research results.</div> Chemistry & Biochemistry https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45351 2026-08-20T10:50:52-04:00 2026-08-20T10:50:53-04:00 ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II <div>Provides support and administrative assistance to the School of Health Sciences (HSC), primarily to the Health Administration (HA) program. This role may also require providing similar support to other HSC department programs beyond HA.</div> Health Sciences, School of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/42260 2025-01-30T10:00:33-05:00 2025-01-30T10:00:33-05:00 ATHLETICS STAFF TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Temporary athletics position. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary athletics positions available. Duties and responsibilities vary based on assignment, which may include camp coach/counselor, color commentator, announcer, play-by-play broadcaster, table crew, working shot clock, on-court host/DJ, academic tutor, athletic trainer, etc.</div> Athletics https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45404 2026-09-01T13:16:21-04:00 2026-09-01T13:16:21-04:00 COORDINATOR - CLERKSHIP / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE <div>The clerkship coordinator is responsible for educational program planning which includes coordinating medical student activities for the Covenant Healthcare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University for year 3 and 4 students, including two core clerkships and multiple elective rotations across a distributed clinical network of a variety of specialties at several medical sites. This position plans and coordinates the routine and ad hoc functions to the clerkship curriculum, including didactics, clinical schedules, faculty recruitment and assignments, along with student orientations and assessment. The coordinator works with the manager of distributed clinical education and serves as the primary point of contact for rotating students, as well as clerkship faculty. This position requires a high degree of professionalism, responsiveness, and attention to detail, as well as the ability to handle/process confidential matters appropriately. In addition, the coordinator operates as task and results oriented in handling multiple priorities, remains flexibility in an evolving work environment, and is open to collaboration.</div> Medicine, College of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45210 2026-07-28T09:21:50-04:00 2026-07-28T09:21:51-04:00 JOURNEYMAN PLUMBER (2 POSITIONS) <div>Performs skilled plumbing work in the installation, maintenance, inspection, and repair, of plumbing systems and related fixtures in accordance with applicable codes, safety standards, and industry best practices. This work involves diagnosing issues, interpreting blueprints, selecting appropriate materials, and ensuring proper functioning of water supply and waste disposal. This position may also coordinate with contractors or other trades and is responsible for ensuring high-quality workmanship, customer service, and compliance with local and state plumbing regulations.</div> Maintenance Mechanics https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45360 2026-08-23T00:04:11-04:00 2026-08-23T00:04:11-04:00 RESEARCH ANALYST / ADVANCEMENT <div>This position supports the fundraising efforts of the university by carrying out proactive and reactive prospect research, database management, prospect and portfolio management and gifts management.</div> Advancement Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/42263 2025-01-30T10:00:41-05:00 2025-01-30T10:00:41-05:00 GYNECOLOGICAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (GTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>In-house training for females to teach the sensitive exam, assess and provide feedback to learners about accurate pelvic, and/or breast examination techniques. The GTA uses their body to guide medical students and physician assistant students through the entire process of performing a thorough pelvic exam: a visual exam (checking for any lumps or bumps), a speculum exam, and a bi-manual exam. The GTAs coach students on their clinical skills and give hands on instruction, as well as comments on technique, language, and overall approach. The GTA also addresses the communication skills needed to provide a comfortable exam in a standardized manner, while using their body as a teaching tool in a supportive, non-threatening environment.</div> Medicine, College of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45408 2026-09-01T14:09:46-04:00 2026-09-01T14:09:46-04:00 ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II/PT <div>Works in a team environment to schedule appointments and perform all check-in processes accurately and appropriately for all CMU Health Services patients (multiple clinics, multiple providers). Enters medical insurance and demographic information into the electronic medical record. Collects copays and past due balances. Performs daily reconciliation and reporting of payments. Stays current on basic health insurance specifics, guidelines, and rules. Maintains the confidentiality, security, and organization of CMU Health Services medical records. Releases patient information as appropriate following HIPAA and FERPA guidelines. Performs a variety of basic office duties.</div> University Health Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45235 2026-07-30T11:25:21-04:00 2026-07-30T11:25:21-04:00 DIRECTOR / RESIDENTIAL EDUCATION <div>Reporting to the Executive Director of Residence Life and Chief Housing Officer, the Director of Residential Education provides strategic, administrative, and organizational leadership for the residential education program serving students across the University’s residence halls and apartment communities.<br><br>The Director is responsible for establishing and advancing a comprehensive residential education strategy that promotes student belonging, learning, well-being, engagement, leadership development, and persistence. The position translates institutional and divisional priorities into coherent residential practices, staffing models, learning experiences, response systems, and performance expectations.<br><br>As a senior leader within Residence Life, the Director moves the Residential Education unit beyond a primarily reactive and relationship-dependent operating model toward one characterized by clear functional ownership, consistent practices, defined decision rights, measurable outcomes, sustainable workloads, and intentional collaboration. The Director evaluates how work is structured and distributed across the unit and implements organizational, procedural, and resource changes necessary to strengthen effectiveness, consistency, accountability, and staff capacity.<br><br>The Director provides leadership for professional and paraprofessional staffing; residential learning and engagement; student leadership development; community standards; crisis and incident response; student care and referral practices; professional development; staff recruitment and retention; and the assessment of residential student outcomes.<br><br>The Director serves as a member of the Residence Life leadership team and works in close partnership with leaders responsible for facilities, housing assignments and operations, student care, assessment, and other departmental functions. The Director also establishes and manages strategic partnerships with campus units whose systems, services, and decisions materially affect the residential student experience.<br><br>This is a live-out position. The Director provides senior-level consultation and escalation support for significant residential incidents and emergencies but does not routinely participate in the primary on-call rotation.</div> Residence Life https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45369 2026-08-25T08:35:43-04:00 2026-08-25T08:35:44-04:00 LANDSCAPE MAINTENANCE OPERATOR I (2 POSITIONS) <div>The Landscape Maintenance Operator keeps campus grounds well maintained, tidy, attractive and presentable year-round, ensuring that students, faculty, and staff can safely move about campus even during inclement weather. This position conducts the planting and routine care of lawns, trees, shrubs, landscape beds, athletic fields, and other campus horticultural spaces. This position may work irregular hours in response to scheduled events, seasonal workloads, and winter storm events, and remains available for campus grounds maintenance related emergencies.</div> Landscape Operations https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/43916 2025-10-28T16:01:10-04:00 2025-10-28T16:01:10-04:00 TEMPORARY MiCAREER MENTOR (PART-TIME) <div>MiCAREER Mentors are experienced educators who guide candidates through the educator credentialing process while fostering professional growth and confidence. Mentors play a vital role in addressing the teacher shortage by supporting candidates’ unique needs and strengthening school communities.</div> Teacher & Special Education https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45413 2026-09-02T09:34:46-04:00 2026-09-02T09:34:46-04:00 COORDINATOR / XR LAB (PART-TIME) <div>The XR lab coordinator will be responsible for scheduling, maintaining, and updating the college of Education and Human Services’ Virtual Reality (VR)/Augmented Reality (AR) (i.e. XR) lab. This includes overseeing any CMU student help in the lab. Additionally, the coordinator will be responsible for programming for the Center for Excellence in STEM Education (Center) that is likely to include XR lab use. These programs are likely to include College Make, Make Shift, Family Make, and K-12 school field trips.</div> Education & Human Svcs, College of https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45248 2026-08-02T00:00:18-04:00 2026-08-02T00:00:20-04:00 BUSINESS & COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT SPECIALIST <div>The business and community development specialist builds partnerships to secure new and steward existing sponsorships, underwriting agreements, and other revenue from businesses and organizations in support of WCMU Public Media. This position contributes to the success of the Development team within Public Broadcasting, providing vital revenue to support WCMU Public Media programs and outreach efforts within the context and culture of philanthropy.</div> Public Broadcasting https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44304 2026-01-27T11:02:21-05:00 2026-01-27T11:02:22-05:00 PROFESSIONAL STAFF TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Temporary professional positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary professional positions available in various departments. Most of these positions require a bachelor’s degree. Duties and responsibilities vary by department but include work requiring consistent exercise of discretion or judgement generally using advanced knowledge. Work may also be directly related to general business operations. Responsibilities may include marketing, communication, graphic design, web site development, project/program coordination, event coordination, data analysis, research, accounting/budget management, student advising, fundraising, etc.</div> HR - Employment Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45371 2026-08-25T10:47:41-04:00 2026-08-25T10:47:41-04:00 TELECOM SPECIALIST I/II/III <div>Responsible for administrative and technical planning for services provided by CMU sub-divisions Unified Communications, OIT and CONNECT/OIT. Duties include programming of a variety of complex communication and security services and other departmental operations and special projects, as assigned. Duties also include providing a high-level customer service experience to all constituents, maintenance of the billing system database and assisting with the management of CMU student employees. Other key aspects of work at this level include a high degree of independence and latitude to make decisions regarding customer credit, decisions regarding the best service plan for a customer, and decisions regarding work assignment prioritization.</div> Connect - OIT https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45415 2026-09-03T10:22:13-04:00 2026-09-03T10:22:13-04:00 COORDINATOR / ATHLETICS EQUIPMENT OPERATIONS <div>Develops, manages and facilities all policies and procedures that relate to football equipment operations in the Athletics Department. Manages an equipment budget for annual purchases including uniforms, helmets, headsets, practice equipment, sideline apparel and other equipment operational needs. Responsible for safety awareness, precautions and compliance as it relates to practice and game day equipment protocols. Provides supervision and training to student managers and others as designated.</div> Athletics - Internal Operations https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45272 2026-08-06T00:00:49-04:00 2026-08-06T00:00:51-04:00 HVACR / CONTROLS TECHNICIAN <div>Performs skilled work in the installation, operation, maintenance and repair of heating, ventilating, air conditioning, and refrigeration systems in addition to HVACR controls and energy management systems.</div> Refrigeration & Control - CEF https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44306 2026-01-27T11:02:27-05:00 2026-01-27T11:02:28-05:00 TECHNICIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) <div>Temporary technician positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary technician positions available in various departments. Duties and responsibilities vary by department but primarily require specialized knowledge, applied scientific or technical skills. Responsibilities may include laboratory support, technical assistance for researchers or the library, medical billing/coding, technical operations assistance related to setup, production and breakdown of events, classroom technical support, printing press support, maintenance, etc.</div> HR - Employment Services https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45375 2026-08-25T14:24:02-04:00 2026-08-25T14:24:02-04:00 ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / FINANCIAL PLANNING & BUDGETS <div>Responsible for financial planning and budgetary matters that arise in the absence of the university budget officer/assistant to the president for strategic planning (UBO) and supports a wide range of financial planning and budget-related matters. This position plays a lead role in budgetary support for the campus community and manages collaborative working relationships and relevant oversight with other campus departments. Additionally, this position assists in the establishment or revision of major objectives and policies in the areas of financial planning, budgeting, resource allocation, training and support, and provides supervision over assigned staff in the Office of Financial Planning and Budgets (FPB).</div> Financial Planning & Budgets https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45285 2026-08-07T10:46:20-04:00 2026-08-07T10:46:21-04:00 CUSTODIAN (8 POSITIONS) <div>Maintains the cleanliness of academic, residential, and administrative campus buildings and service areas. Performs manual custodial tasks in university buildings. Ensures spaces are presentable and sanitary for employees and visitors.</div> Building Services - GF https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45419 2026-09-03T13:51:35-04:00 2026-09-03T13:51:36-04:00 ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT III <div>This position is the key administrative support person for the Office of Curriculum and Instructional Support (CIS) and assists with administrative tasks for the Executive Director and CIS unit heads. This role requires a high level of professionalism, accuracy in detail, and the ability to maintain confidentiality. The individual performs a variety of functions requiring decision-making and independence of thought and action. This position will serve as a liaison with all CMU constituents for CIS and must be conversant in university procedures and policies relating to the unit’s role and functions. This position assists with various meetings and committees where needed. This position requires independence with a high degree of autonomy/responsibility for complex duties that may be broad and varied or narrow and focused.</div> Curriculum & Instructional Support https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44659 2026-03-25T00:00:54-04:00 2026-03-25T00:00:54-04:00 SENIOR ENERGY FACILITY OPERATOR <div>Performs skilled work in the operation and maintenance of high pressure steam boilers, steam absorption and centrifugal chillers, air conditioning cooling towers, steam, diesel and gas turbine driven generators, air compressors, pumps, and related work as required.</div> Utility Operations https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45385 2026-08-27T14:05:45-04:00 2026-08-27T14:05:45-04:00 ASSISTANT DIRECTOR/COMMUNICATION & ED OUTREACH <div>Supports the Center with communications, social media efforts, and the production of marketing materials that advance the Center's initiatives. Supports outreach efforts through the facilitation of programming for high school students.</div> Gov John Engler Center for Charter Schls"
    },
