APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III Applications & Systems - OIT Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Application Administrator supports the administration, maintenance, security, and continuous improvement of enterprise applications and related systems used across Central Michigan University. Working as part of a collaborative team, this position helps ensure these services are reliable, secure, and effective for the faculty, staff, and students who depend on them. The role includes techni... View Details Bookmark SUPERVISOR / ARCHITECTURAL TRADES Architectural Trades Supervisory Technical 5 External 09/15/2026 Supervises and coordinates activities of employees in the architectural trades, including but not limited to carpentry, painting, locksmith, and masonry trades in the maintenance and renovation of campus facilities. This position also oversees projects related to commercial roofing installation and repair. Must have the ability to be on-call and able to respond to emergency situations in a time... View Details Bookmark ATHLETICS STAFF TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Athletics Temporary Staff 00 External Temporary athletics position. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary athletics positions available. Duties and responsibilities vary based on assignment, which may include camp coach/counselor, color commentator, announcer, play-by-play broadcaster, table crew, working shot clock, on-court host/DJ, academic tutor, athletic trainer, etc. View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / ATHLETICS EQUIPMENT OPERATIONS Athletics - Internal Operations Professional & Administrative -Salary External 09/17/2026 Develops, manages and facilities all policies and procedures that relate to football equipment operations in the Athletics Department. Manages an equipment budget for annual purchases including uniforms, helmets, headsets, practice equipment, sideline apparel and other equipment operational needs. Responsible for safety awareness, precautions and compliance as it relates to practice and game da... View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE ATHLETIC TRAINER Athletics - Sports Medicine Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Associate Athletic Trainer is a certified and licensed healthcare professional responsible for delivering comprehensive athletic training services to Central Michigan University (CMU) intercollegiate student-athletes. This position plays an integral role within the Sports Medicine team and reports to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. View Details Bookmark CUSTODIAN (8 POSITIONS) Building Services Service Maintenance 2 External Maintains the cleanliness of academic, residential, and administrative campus buildings and service areas. Performs manual custodial tasks in university buildings. Ensures spaces are presentable and sanitary for employees and visitors. View Details Bookmark JOURNEYMAN CARPENTER (2 POSITIONS) Carpentry Shop Service Maintenance 8 External Performs skilled work in the construction, maintenance and repair of structures, equipment and articles of wood; performs related work as required. View Details Bookmark DIRECTOR/ASSESSMENT & EVALUATION Charter Schools for Gov John Engler Center Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is responsible for leading The Center for Charter School’s functions associated with the analysis and use of data, evaluation of the performance of authorized schools, and oversight of school assessment practices. The Director of Assessment & Evaluation (DAE) ensures that relevant staff have the information they need to make decisions regarding academic school performance and ... View Details Bookmark BOOKSTORE TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) CMU Bookstore Temporary Staff 00 External Temporary bookstore positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary bookstore positions available. Charges CMU Bookstore customers for their purchases using credit and debit cards, student accounts, checks and cash using a point-of-sale (POS) register. Helps students find their books, re-shelves books, and straightens shelves. Buys back books at the end of the semesters. View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE CMU Online Professional & Administrative -Salary External The associate director of marketing operations for CMU Online is an operations-focused role responsible for driving the organization, coordination, and execution of integrated marketing efforts that support online and adult learners. This position manages the development and delivery of full-funnel marketing content across digital (web, social, email) and print channels, ensuring work moves eff... View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT/CMU ONLINE CMU ONLINE Senior Officer External The Associate Vice President (AVP) has oversight of the academic unit within the CMU Online Learning enterprise. In partnership with academic colleges, departments, and university stakeholders, the AVP supports the development, delivery, and growth of online, hybrid, and off-campus academic and professional learning opportunities. The AVP collaborates with faculty and academic leadership to adv... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / DESIGN & VISUAL MEDIA CMU Online Professional & Administrative -Salary External The assistant director of design and visual media for CMU Online is a design-focused role responsible for creating and delivering high-quality visual and multimedia assets that support integrated marketing efforts for online and adult learners. This position produces audience-centered creative across digital channels (web, social, email, and video) and print materials (brochures, flyers, and re... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / PROFESSIONAL LEARNING PROGRAM College of Education & Human Services Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Center for Excellence in STEM Education (CESE) Assistant Director of Professional Learning Program provides support in professional learning experiences, research, grant writing and publications within the College of Education and Human Services’ Center for Excellence in STEM Education. View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / XR LAB (PART-TIME) College of Education & Human Services Supervisory Technical 4 External The XR lab coordinator will be responsible for scheduling, maintaining, and updating the college of Education and Human Services’ Virtual Reality (VR)/Augmented Reality (AR) (i.e. XR) lab. This includes overseeing any CMU student help in the lab. Additionally, the coordinator will be responsible for programming for the Center for Excellence in STEM Education (Center) that is likely to include X... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR - RECRUITMENT / COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SOCIAL SCIENCES College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences Professional & Administrative -Salary External Under the supervision of the dean, the coordinator of recruiting is responsible for planning, coordinating, and staffing the College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences (CLASS) recruiting events and for building strong working relationships across the University to grow CLASS enrollment. The coordinator serves as the college’s primary liaison to CMU Admissions and works closely with Academic ... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR - STANDARDIZED PATIENT SIMULATION CENTER / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE College of Medicine Professional & Administrative -Hourly External This position assists with coordination and supervision of the daily events and activities of the Standardized Patient-Simulation Center, on and off campus. This position will assist internal and external clientele to fulfill the needs of the program and plan future events. Responsibilities include assessing and managing problems on and off-site, monitoring quality assurance of events, promotin... View Details Bookmark MALE UROGENITAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (MUTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) College of Medicine Temporary Staff 00 External In-house training for males to teach, assess, and provide feedback to learners about accurate urogenital and rectal examination techniques. The MUTA addresses the communication skills needed to provide a comfortable exam in a standardized manner, while using their body as a teaching tool in a supportive, non-threatening environment. The MUTA teaches the proper technique for performing the uroge... View Details Bookmark CLINICAL RESEARCH NURSE / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE College of Medicine Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is comprised of both clinical and regulatory responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include assisting with developing and implementing the activities of a clinical research trial which consists of pre-screening patients for study eligibility and performing delegated study tasks including but not limited to: treatment procedures, drawing blood, performing EKGs, administrat... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR - CLERKSHIP / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE College of Medicine Professional & Administrative -Hourly External The clerkship coordinator is responsible for educational program planning which includes coordinating medical student activities for the Covenant Healthcare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University for year 3 and 4 students, including two core clerkships and multiple elective rotations across a distributed clinical network of a variety of specialties at several medical sites. This pos... View Details Bookmark GYNECOLOGICAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (GTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) College of Medicine Temporary Staff 00 External In-house training for females to teach the sensitive exam, assess and provide feedback to learners about accurate pelvic, and/or breast examination techniques. The GTA uses their body to guide medical students and physician assistant students through the entire process of performing a thorough pelvic exam: a visual exam (checking for any lumps or bumps), a speculum exam, and a bi-manual exam. T... View Details Bookmark TELECOM SPECIALIST I/II/III Connect - OIT Supervisory Technical External 09/08/2026 Responsible for administrative and technical planning for services provided by CMU sub-divisions Unified Communications, OIT and CONNECT/OIT. Duties include programming of a variety of complex communication and security services and other departmental operations and special projects, as assigned. Duties also include providing a high-level customer service experience to all constituents, mainten... View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT III Curriculum & Instructional Support Administrative Office Assistant External This position is the key administrative support person for the Office of Curriculum and Instructional Support (CIS) and assists with administrative tasks for the Executive Director and CIS unit heads. This role requires a high level of professionalism, accuracy in detail, and the ability to maintain confidentiality. The individual performs a variety of functions requiring decision-making and in... View Details Bookmark Synthesis and Chemical Biology of Mycobacterial Glycolipids Postdoctoral Research Fellow Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry Postdoctoral Research Fellow External One postdoctoral research fellow position focused on the synthesis and chemical biology of mycobacterial glycolipids is available starting September 1, 2026, in the laboratory of Dr. Ben Swarts in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Central Michigan University. The initial appointment for this position is one year, with the expectation of renewal, contingent upon funding and satisfa... View Details Bookmark Assistant Women's Basketball Coach Department of Intercollegiate Athletics Athletic Coach (Faculty) N/A External Duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to, assisting with organization and administration of the women’s basketball program including practice and game coaching, recruiting, scouting, social media and public relations. View Details Bookmark X-ray Studies of Quantum Materials