ural characterization of quantum materials using x-ray scattering techniques and structure modeling. View Details Bookmark Synthesis and Chemical Biology of Mycobacterial Glycolipids Postdoctoral Research Fellow Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry Postdoctoral Research Fellow External One postdoctoral research fellow position focused on the synthesis and chemical biology of mycobacterial glycolipids is available starting September 1, 2026, in the laboratory of Dr. Ben Swarts in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Central Michigan University. The initial appointment for this position is one year, with the expectation of renewal, contingent upon funding and satisfa... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR - STANDARDIZED PATIENT SIMULATION CENTER / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE College of Medicine Professional & Administrative -Hourly External This position assists with coordination and supervision of the daily events and activities of the Standardized Patient-Simulation Center, on and off campus. This position will assist internal and external clientele to fulfill the needs of the program and plan future events. Responsibilities include assessing and managing problems on and off-site, monitoring quality assurance of events, promotin... View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE CMU Online Professional & Administrative -Salary External The associate director of marketing operations for CMU Online is an operations-focused role responsible for driving the organization, coordination, and execution of integrated marketing efforts that support online and adult learners. This position manages the development and delivery of full-funnel marketing content across digital (web, social, email) and print channels, ensuring work moves eff... View Details Bookmark TEMPORARY MASON (PART-TIME) Masonry Shop Temporary Staff External Performs skilled work in the construction, repair and maintenance of masonry structures; performs related work as required. View Details Bookmark DIRECTOR/ASSESSMENT & EVALUATION Charter Schools for Gov John Engler Center Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is responsible for leading The Center for Charter School’s functions associated with the analysis and use of data, evaluation of the performance of authorized schools, and oversight of school assessment practices. The Director of Assessment & Evaluation (DAE) ensures that relevant staff have the information they need to make decisions regarding academic school performance and ... View Details Bookmark PROJECT ADVISOR / UPWARD BOUND (2 POSITIONS) TRIO Programs - Detroit Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is located in Detroit, Michigan and serves students within a Detroit Public Schools Community District High School and Charter Schools. The Project Advisor position is a federally-funded TRIO program providing opportunities for participants to succeed in their precollege performance and ultimately in their higher education pursuits. The Project Advisor assists in planning, impleme... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / RISK MANAGEMENT, ENVIRONMENTAL HEALTH & SAFETY Risk Management, Environmental Health & Safety Professional & Administrative -Salary External Under general supervision, develops, implements and maintains environmental, health and safety programs in support of the University’s mission and in compliance with university policies, procedures, state and federal regulations and standards to ensure the environmental health and safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Works in coordination with campus community while providing guida... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / ALTERNATIVE BREAKS Volunteer Center Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Assistant Director of the Mary Ellen Brandell Volunteer Center (VC) will work collaboratively with the Director and other professional staff and student members of the Volunteer Center to develop, support, and promote service opportunities to engage students with the mission and values of Central Michigan University. The Assistant Director will serve as the university advisor to the Alterna... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / CEREMONIES & EVENTS President's Office Professional & Administrative -Salary External Reporting to the chief of staff to the president, the ceremonies and events coordinator is responsible for the development, management, oversight, execution, and assessment of all events led by the Office of the President. The coordinator works collaboratively with stakeholders across and external to the university to execute event planning and logistics. This position also maintains the Office... View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II/PT University Health Services Administrative Office Assistant External Works in a team environment to schedule appointments and perform all check-in processes accurately and appropriately for all CMU Health Services patients (multiple clinics, multiple providers). Enters medical insurance and demographic information into the electronic medical record. Collects copays and past due balances. Performs daily reconciliation and reporting of payments. Stays current on b... View Details Bookmark CUSTODIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Facilities Management Temporary Staff External Temporary custodian positions. No benefits. A custodian is the key University and Facilities Management person in maintaining cleanliness of academic, residential, and administrative campus buildings and service areas. Performs manual custodial tasks in care of University buildings; performs related work as required. View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II Risk Mgmt, Environmental Health & Safety Administrative Office Assistant External This position is responsible for providing administrative support to the Office of Environmental Health & Safety/Emergency Management a part of the Risk Management, Environmental Health & Safety unit. The person in this position must be able to work at a high degree of independence while supporting multiple staff members including coordinating meetings, developing and distributing meeti... View Details Bookmark AUDITOR / SENIOR AUDITOR Internal Audit Professional & Administrative -Salary External Reporting to the Director of Internal Audit, this position plans, performs, and documents risk-based operational, financial, information technology, and compliance audits and other projects independently to evaluate university governance, risk management, and control processes. This position performs all phases of audits/investigations including conducting an audit risk assessment, conducting a... View Details Bookmark MEDICAL SUPPORT STAFF POOL (RN, CMA, RMA, LPN) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) University Health Services Temporary Staff External Under the supervision of full-time medical staff, individuals in this role support the daily operations of the Student Health Services Clinic or Primary Specialty Clinic. Responsibilities are determined by the licensure and qualifications of the individual and include direct patient care and administrative support. The clinic provides a broad range of services, including routine medical care, p... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / PROFESSIONAL LEARNING PROGRAM College of Education & Human Services Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Center for Excellence in STEM Education (CESE) Assistant Director of Professional Learning Program provides support in professional learning experiences, research, grant writing and publications within the College of Education and Human Services’ Center for Excellence in STEM Education. View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT/CMU ONLINE CMU ONLINE Senior Officer External The Associate Vice President (AVP) has oversight of the academic unit within the CMU Online Learning enterprise. In partnership with academic colleges, departments, and university stakeholders, the AVP supports the development, delivery, and growth of online, hybrid, and off-campus academic and professional learning opportunities. The AVP collaborates with faculty and academic leadership to adv... View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Various Temporary Staff External Part-time temporary administrative office assistant positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary administrative office assistant positions available in various departments. Duties and responsibilities vary by department but are primarily focused on providing secretarial support for specific departments. Responsibilities may include scheduling meetings, answering the phone, drafting co... View Details Bookmark CLINICAL RESEARCH NURSE / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE College of Medicine Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is comprised of both clinical and regulatory responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include assisting with developing and implementing the activities of a clinical research trial which consists of pre-screening patients for study eligibility and performing delegated study tasks including but not limited to: treatment procedures, drawing blood, performing EKGs, administrat... View Details Bookmark MANAGER/LIBRARY SYSTEMS Libraries - Library Systems Professional & Administrative -Salary External Provides strategic leadership, coordination, and operational expertise for University Libraries’ systems in a collaborative, service oriented environment. This 12 month, non tenure track librarian position is responsible for the planning, implementation, oversight, and continued evolution of library systems across their full lifecycle, ensuring reliable services that align with library and univ... View Details Bookmark APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III Applications & Systems - OIT Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Application Administrator supports the administration, maintenance, security, and continuous improvement of enterprise applications and related systems used across Central Michigan University. Working as part of a collaborative team, this position helps ensure these services are reliable, secure, and effective for the faculty, staff, and students who depend on them. The role includes techni... View Details Bookmark ACADEMIC TUTOR/FACILITATOR TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) TRIO PROGRAMS - DETROIT Temporary Staff External Provides academic assistance to students in all academic areas and workshop facilitation as needed. Tutors work with TRIO Detroit Upward Bound and Educational Talent Search programs in Southwest and Northwest, Detroit within our target schools. View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / TEACHER & SPECIAL EDUCATION PREPARATION PATHWAYS Teacher & Special Education Professional & Administrative -Salary External The teacher and special education preparation pathways coordinator works in the Department of Teacher and Special Education at Central Michigan University and supports multiple educator preparation pathway programs. This position provides leadership and coordination for program operations, candidate advising, recruitment, reporting, clinical placement processes, and accreditation-related activi... View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT III Economics Administrative Office Assistant INTERNAL -Primary support person for department, including MA in Economics Graduate Program -Primarily responsible for day-to-day office operations, including supervision of student assistants -Primarily responsible for maintaining and analyzing budgetary records, including ProfEd off-campus and online tuition and expenses, faculty grants and professional development accounts -Primarily responsible for ... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / DESIGN & VISUAL MEDIA CMU Online Professional & Administrative -Salary External The assistant director of design and visual media for CMU Online is a design-focused role responsible for creating and delivering high-quality visual and multimedia assets that support integrated marketing efforts for online and adult learners. This position produces audience-centered creative across digital channels (web, social, email, and video) and print materials (brochures, flyers, and re... View Details Bookmark VICE PRES/RESEARCH & SPONSORED PROGRAMS RESEARCH & SPONSORED PROGRAMS Senior Officer External Central Michigan University (CMU) is classified as a Carnegie Research 2 (R2): High Research Spending and Doctorate Production institution, with high research activity and doctoral education. The Vice President for Research and Sponsored Programs (VPRSP) reports to the Provost/Executive Vice President and provides senior leadership across the university to develop and implement a clear vision f... View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE ATHLETIC TRAINER Athletics - Sports Medicine Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Associate Athletic Trainer is a certified and licensed healthcare professional responsible for delivering comprehensive athletic training services to Central Michigan University (CMU) intercollegiate student-athletes. This position plays an integral role within the Sports Medicine team and reports to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. View Details Bookmark INSTALL REPAIR TECH I/II - OIT Telecommunication Services-OIT Supervisory Technical External Responsible for installation, removal, rearrangement and maintenance on a variety of complex communication and security equipment. May repair and/or add to the University’s switch and database. View Details Bookmark INDUSTRIAL HYGIENIST TEMPORARY Laboratory & Field Safety Temporary Staff External Temporary position. No benefits. Assists the Director of the Office of Laboratory and Field Safety with implementing various lab safety programs on campus. Works in coordination with campus community while providing laboratory safety services (chemical, biological, radiological, and laser). View Details Bookmark Go to search