ained, tidy, attractive and presentable year-round, ensuring that students, faculty, and staff can safely move about campus even during inclement weather. This position conducts the planting and routine care of lawns, trees, shrubs, landscape beds, athletic fields, and other campus horticultural spaces. This position may work irr... View Details Bookmark TEMPORARY MiCAREER MENTOR (PART-TIME) Teacher & Special Education Temporary Staff 00 External MiCAREER Mentors are experienced educators who guide candidates through the educator credentialing process while fostering professional growth and confidence. Mentors play a vital role in addressing the teacher shortage by supporting candidates’ unique needs and strengthening school communities. View Details Bookmark BUSINESS & COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT SPECIALIST Public Broadcasting Public Broadcasting - Salary 3 External The business and community development specialist builds partnerships to secure new and steward existing sponsorships, underwriting agreements, and other revenue from businesses and organizations in support of WCMU Public Media. This position contributes to the success of the Development team within Public Broadcasting, providing vital revenue to support WCMU Public Media programs and outreach ... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / XR LAB (PART-TIME) College of Education & Human Services Supervisory Technical 4 External The XR lab coordinator will be responsible for scheduling, maintaining, and updating the college of Education and Human Services’ Virtual Reality (VR)/Augmented Reality (AR) (i.e. XR) lab. This includes overseeing any CMU student help in the lab. Additionally, the coordinator will be responsible for programming for the Center for Excellence in STEM Education (Center) that is likely to include X... View Details Bookmark TELECOM SPECIALIST I/II/III Connect - OIT Supervisory Technical External 09/08/2026 Responsible for administrative and technical planning for services provided by CMU sub-divisions Unified Communications, OIT and CONNECT/OIT. Duties include programming of a variety of complex communication and security services and other departmental operations and special projects, as assigned. Duties also include providing a high-level customer service experience to all constituents, mainten... View Details Bookmark PROFESSIONAL STAFF TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Various Temporary Staff External Temporary professional positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary professional positions available in various departments. Most of these positions require a bachelor’s degree. Duties and responsibilities vary by department but include work requiring consistent exercise of discretion or judgement generally using advanced knowledge. Work may also be directly related to general busines... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / ATHLETICS EQUIPMENT OPERATIONS Athletics - Internal Operations Professional & Administrative -Salary External 09/17/2026 Develops, manages and facilities all policies and procedures that relate to football equipment operations in the Athletics Department. Manages an equipment budget for annual purchases including uniforms, helmets, headsets, practice equipment, sideline apparel and other equipment operational needs. Responsible for safety awareness, precautions and compliance as it relates to practice and game da... View Details Bookmark HVACR / CONTROLS TECHNICIAN Refrigeration & Control - Central Energy Facility Service Maintenance 10 External Performs skilled work in the installation, operation, maintenance and repair of heating, ventilating, air conditioning, and refrigeration systems in addition to HVACR controls and energy management systems. View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / FINANCIAL PLANNING & BUDGETS Financial Planning & Budgets Professional & Administrative -Salary External Responsible for financial planning and budgetary matters that arise in the absence of the university budget officer/assistant to the president for strategic planning (UBO) and supports a wide range of financial planning and budget-related matters. This position plays a lead role in budgetary support for the campus community and manages collaborative working relationships and relevant oversight ... View Details Bookmark TECHNICIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Various Temporary Staff External Temporary technician positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary technician positions available in various departments. Duties and responsibilities vary by department but primarily require specialized knowledge, applied scientific or technical skills. Responsibilities may include laboratory support, technical assistance for researchers or the library, medical billing/coding, technica... View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT III Curriculum & Instructional Support Administrative Office Assistant External This position is the key administrative support person for the Office of Curriculum and Instructional Support (CIS) and assists with administrative tasks for the Executive Director and CIS unit heads. This role requires a high level of professionalism, accuracy in detail, and the ability to maintain confidentiality. The individual performs a variety of functions requiring decision-making and in... View Details Bookmark CUSTODIAN (8 POSITIONS) Building Services Service Maintenance 2 External Maintains the cleanliness of academic, residential, and administrative campus buildings and service areas. Performs manual custodial tasks in university buildings. Ensures spaces are presentable and sanitary for employees and visitors. View Details Bookmark Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 3 Next Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution.  CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, ge