ark Bachelor of Science in Nursing Lecturer School of Rehabilitation and Medical Sciences Fixed-Term Faculty - Academic Year External The Nursing Program at Central Michigan University invites applications for a full-time fixed-term faculty position beginning in August 2026 for the Fall 2026 semester. The successful candidate will provide instructional leadership in maternity and pediatric nursing, including didactic teaching and oversight of clinical instructors assigned to related clinical courses. The faculty member will a... View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE CMU Online Professional & Administrative -Salary External The associate director of marketing operations for CMU Online is an operations-focused role responsible for driving the organization, coordination, and execution of integrated marketing efforts that support online and adult learners. This position manages the development and delivery of full-funnel marketing content across digital (web, social, email) and print channels, ensuring work moves eff... View Details Bookmark TEMPORARY MASON (PART-TIME) Masonry Shop Temporary Staff External Performs skilled work in the construction, repair and maintenance of masonry structures; performs related work as required. View Details Bookmark PROJECT ADVISOR / UPWARD BOUND (2 POSITIONS) TRIO Programs - Detroit Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is located in Detroit, Michigan and serves students within a Detroit Public Schools Community District High School and Charter Schools. The Project Advisor position is a federally-funded TRIO program providing opportunities for participants to succeed in their precollege performance and ultimately in their higher education pursuits. The Project Advisor assists in planning, impleme... View Details Bookmark DIRECTOR/ASSESSMENT & EVALUATION Charter Schools for Gov John Engler Center Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is responsible for leading The Center for Charter School’s functions associated with the analysis and use of data, evaluation of the performance of authorized schools, and oversight of school assessment practices. The Director of Assessment & Evaluation (DAE) ensures that relevant staff have the information they need to make decisions regarding academic school performance and ... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / RISK MANAGEMENT, ENVIRONMENTAL HEALTH & SAFETY Risk Management, Environmental Health & Safety Professional & Administrative -Salary External Under general supervision, develops, implements and maintains environmental, health and safety programs in support of the University’s mission and in compliance with university policies, procedures, state and federal regulations and standards to ensure the environmental health and safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Works in coordination with campus community while providing guida... View Details Bookmark BOOKSTORE TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) CMU Bookstore Temporary Staff 00 External Temporary bookstore positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary bookstore positions available. Charges CMU Bookstore customers for their purchases using credit and debit cards, student accounts, checks and cash using a point-of-sale (POS) register. Helps students find their books, re-shelves books, and straightens shelves. Buys back books at the end of the semesters. View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / ALTERNATIVE BREAKS Volunteer Center Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Assistant Director of the Mary Ellen Brandell Volunteer Center (VC) will work collaboratively with the Director and other professional staff and student members of the Volunteer Center to develop, support, and promote service opportunities to engage students with the mission and values of Central Michigan University. The Assistant Director will serve as the university advisor to the Alterna... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / CEREMONIES & EVENTS President's Office Professional & Administrative -Salary External Reporting to the chief of staff to the president, the ceremonies and events coordinator is responsible for the development, management, oversight, execution, and assessment of all events led by the Office of the President. The coordinator works collaboratively with stakeholders across and external to the university to execute event planning and logistics. This position also maintains the Office... View Details Bookmark MALE UROGENITAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (MUTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) College of Medicine Temporary Staff 00 External In-house training for males to teach, assess, and provide feedback to learners about accurate urogenital and rectal examination techniques. The MUTA addresses the communication skills needed to provide a comfortable exam in a standardized manner, while using their body as a teaching tool in a supportive, non-threatening environment. The MUTA teaches the proper technique for performing the uroge... View Details Bookmark CUSTODIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Facilities Management Temporary Staff External Temporary custodian positions. No benefits. A custodian is the key University and Facilities Management person in maintaining cleanliness of academic, residential, and administrative campus buildings and service areas. Performs manual custodial tasks in care of University buildings; performs related work as required. View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II/PT University Health Services Administrative Office Assistant External Works in a team environment to schedule appointments and perform all check-in processes accurately and appropriately for all CMU Health Services patients (multiple clinics, multiple providers). Enters medical insurance and demographic information into the electronic medical record. Collects copays and past due balances. Performs daily reconciliation and reporting of payments. Stays current on b... View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II Risk Mgmt, Environmental Health & Safety Administrative Office Assistant External This position is responsible for providing administrative support to the Office of Environmental Health & Safety/Emergency Management a part of the Risk Management, Environmental Health & Safety unit. The person in this position must be able to work at a high degree of independence while supporting multiple staff members including coordinating meetings, developing and distributing meeti... View Details Bookmark CHP STANDARDIZED PATIENT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) The HH & GA Dow College of Health Prof IPEP Center Temporary Staff 00 External Standardized patient simulation involves the use of individuals trained to portray the roles of patients, family members or others to allow students the opportunity to develop, practice and enhance their interviewing skills, communication skills, physical exam/evaluations, and history taking techniques. Students participate in multiple standardized patient exercises throughout their healthcare ... View Details Bookmark AUDITOR / SENIOR AUDITOR Internal Audit Professional & Administrative -Salary External Reporting to the Director of Internal Audit, this position plans, performs, and documents risk-based operational, financial, information technology, and compliance audits and other projects independently to evaluate university governance, risk management, and control processes. This position performs all phases of audits/investigations including conducting an audit risk assessment, conducting a... View Details Bookmark PHYSICS/MACHINE SHOP TECHNICIAN II Physics Supervisory Technical 4 External Responsible for setting up and disassembling instructional laboratories, repairs and maintains laboratory equipment, controls departmental supply and equipment inventory, uses machine and wood shop techniques to fabricate and/or modify instructional and research equipment. View Details Bookmark MEDICAL SUPPORT STAFF POOL (RN, CMA, RMA, LPN) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) University Health Services Temporary Staff External Under the supervision of full-time medical staff, individuals in this role support the daily operations of the Student Health Services Clinic or Primary Specialty Clinic. Responsibilities are determined by the licensure and qualifications of the individual and include direct patient care and administrative support. The clinic provides a broad range of services, including routine medical care, p... View Details Bookmark X-ray Studies of Quantum Materials Postdoctoral Research Fellow Department of Physics Postdoctoral Research Fellow External A postdoctoral position is available starting February 1, 2026, in the Physics Department at Central Michigan University. We are seeking an enthusiastic scientist to work in the field of structural characterization of quantum materials using x-ray scattering techniques and structure modeling. View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / PROFESSIONAL LEARNING PROGRAM College of Education & Human Services Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Center for Excellence in STEM Education (CESE) Assistant Director of Professional Learning Program provides support in professional learning experiences, research, grant writing and publications within the College of Education and Human Services’ Center for Excellence in STEM Education. View Details Bookmark JOURNEYMAN CARPENTER (2 POSITIONS) Carpentry Shop Service Maintenance 8 External Performs skilled work in the construction, maintenance and repair of structures, equipment and articles of wood; performs related work as required. View Details Bookmark ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT/CMU ONLINE CMU ONLINE Senior Officer External The Associate Vice President (AVP) has oversight of the academic unit within the CMU Online Learning enterprise. In partnership with academic colleges, departments, and university stakeholders, the AVP supports the development, delivery, and growth of online, hybrid, and off-campus academic and professional learning opportunities. The AVP collaborates with faculty and academic leadership to adv... View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Various Temporary Staff External Part-time temporary administrative office assistant positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary administrative office assistant positions available in various departments. Duties and responsibilities vary by department but are primarily focused on providing secretarial support for specific departments. Responsibilities may include scheduling meetings, answering the phone, drafting co... View Details Bookmark CLINICAL RESEARCH NURSE / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE College of Medicine Professional & Administrative -Salary External This position is comprised of both clinical and regulatory responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include assisting with developing and implementing the activities of a clinical research trial which consists of pre-screening patients for study eligibility and performing delegated study tasks including but not limited to: treatment procedures, drawing blood, performing EKGs, administrat... View Details Bookmark MANAGER/LIBRARY SYSTEMS Libraries - Library Systems Professional & Administrative -Salary External Provides strategic leadership, coordination, and operational expertise for University Libraries’ systems in a collaborative, service oriented environment. This 12 month, non tenure track librarian position is responsible for the planning, implementation, oversight, and continued evolution of library systems across their full lifecycle, ensuring reliable services that align with library and univ... View Details Bookmark APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III Applications & Systems - OIT Professional & Administrative -Salary External The Application Administrator supports the administration, maintenance, security, and continuous improvement of enterprise applications and related systems used across Central Michigan University. Working as part of a collaborative team, this position helps ensure these services are reliable, secure, and effective for the faculty, staff, and students who depend on them. The role includes techni... View Details Bookmark ACADEMIC TUTOR/FACILITATOR TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) TRIO PROGRAMS - DETROIT Temporary Staff External Provides academic assistance to students in all academic areas and workshop facilitation as needed. Tutors work with TRIO Detroit Upward Bound and Educational Talent Search programs in Southwest and Northwest, Detroit within our target schools. View Details Bookmark ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT III Economics Administrative Office Assistant INTERNAL -Primary support person for department, including MA in Economics Graduate Program -Primarily responsible for day-to-day office operations, including supervision of student assistants -Primarily responsible for maintaining and analyzing budgetary records, including ProfEd off-campus and online tuition and expenses, faculty grants and professional development accounts -Primarily responsible for ... View Details Bookmark COORDINATOR / TEACHER & SPECIAL EDUCATION PREPARATION PATHWAYS Teacher & Special Education Professional & Administrative -Salary External The teacher and special education preparation pathways coordinator works in the Department of Teacher and Special Education at Central Michigan University and supports multiple educator preparation pathway programs. This position provides leadership and coordination for program operations, candidate advising, recruitment, reporting, clinical placement processes, and accreditation-related activi... View Details Bookmark Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 3 Next Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution.  CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright © Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
