      "title": "CMU Applicant Portal",
      "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Log In Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary’s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Your session has expired. Please log in. Log In Required fields are indicated with an asterisk * Username * Password * Forgot your username or password? Or Create an Account × The Chronicle of Higher Education had retired the \"Apply with Vitae\" login option. No need to worry, read on for steps to access your account. To access the account, return to the login page using the \"X\" in the upper corner or clicking outside of this pop-up box. Use the \"Forgot your username or password?\" link with your original Chronicle Vitae username to create a new password and access your account. Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution.  CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright © Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45390": {
      "title": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE",
      "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary’s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU’s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. *This position is available in Mt. Pleasant, Troy, Grand Rapids, or Traverse City. The work location for this position is negotiable based on the selected candidate's qualifications, business needs, and operational requirements. Flexible work arrangements, including remote, hybrid, or on-site work, may be considered where appropriate. The accompanying salary offer will be determined based on candidate’s work location. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3936 Position Number 78480 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR, MARKETING OPERATIONS / CMU ONLINE Position Summary The associate director of marketing operations for CMU Online is an operations-focused role responsible for driving the organization, coordination, and execution of integrated marketing efforts that support online and adult learners. This position manages the development and delivery of full-funnel marketing content across digital (web, social, email) and print channels, ensuring work moves efficiently from concept through to completion. While contributing to content direction and writing as needed, the primary focus is maintaining momentum by keeping projects on track, aligning stakeholders, and ensuring timely execution. Working in close collaboration with CMU Online’s marketing director, the associate director plays a key role in coordinating campaigns, managing timelines, and ensuring marketing efforts are delivered effectively, aligned with audience needs, and supportive of CMU Online’s enrollment goals. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, journalism, public relations, or a related field. Two years of professional marketing experience with demonstrated success executing multi-channel marketing efforts. Demonstrated experience developing and managing content across multiple platforms, including social media (LinkedIn, Meta), web, email/ CRM systems, blogs, and print/traditional marketing materials. Demonstrated experience working with CRM platforms (e.g., Slate) to support email communications, audience segmentation, and campaign execution. Demonstrated experience collaborating with cross-functional teams and managing projects across multiple stakeholders and priorities. Strong writing and storytelling skills with the ability to develop clear, engaging, and audience-focused content across formats. Exceptional organizational and project management skills, with a demonstrated ability to manage multiple concurrent projects, maintain detailed content calendars, and ensure timely execution of campaigns. Ability to balance creative thinking with operational discipline, contributing to content development while ensuring projects move forward efficiently and do not stall. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in marketing, communications, journalism, public relations, or a related field; or progressively advanced experience in a related field. Demonstrated experience developing marketing content for higher education or adult learner audiences. Familiarity with Sitefinity or similar content management systems. Demonstrated understanding of social media performance metrics and content optimization best practices. Demonstrated experience supporting multi-channel campaigns that include email, social media, web, and print content. Demonstrated experience coordinating with third-party service providers (e.g., printers, agencies). Relevant certification(s) in digital marketing, content marketing, or analytics platforms. Duties & Responsibilities Develops, creates, and manages high-quality marketing content across social media, blog, web, email, and print/traditional channels, including flyers, brochures, and other recruitment collateral. Executes and optimizes CRM and email communications using Slate, including campaign setup, segmentation support, and content development. Develops and maintains a comprehensive content calendar for CMU Online in collaboration with the marketing director, ensuring alignment with campaign priorities and institutional initiatives. Coordinates the execution of integrated marketing campaigns across multiple channels (digital and print), ensuring timelines are met and deliverables are completed. Contributes to content ideation and creative direction in partnership with marketing leadership, while maintaining a focus on execution and delivery. Collaborates closely with the University Marketing and Communications office and other internal stakeholders to ensure alignment with institutional messaging, priorities, and processes. Works cross-functionally with teams across CMU Online (e.g., student services, business and community outreach, Central Bound) to gather content, support initiatives, and align messaging. Assists in coordinating external vendors as needed to support campaign execution and content production. Monitors campaign timelines, workflows, and deliverables to ensure projects remain on track and do not stall. Supports ongoing updates and enhancements to CMU Online web and landing page content. Tracks and reviews basic performance metrics across digital channels to inform content improvements and campaign adjustments. Ensures all marketing content reflects the appropriate tone, clarity, accuracy, and audience alignment. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU’s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. *This position is available in Mt. Pleasant, Troy, Grand Rapids, or Traverse City. The work location for this position is negotiable based on the selected candidate’s qualifications, business needs, and operational requirements. Flexible work arrangements, including remote, hybrid, or on-site work, may be considered where appropriate. The accompanying salary offer will be determined based on candidate’s work location. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $66,000 - $86,600* Division Academic Affairs Department CMU Online Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, Traverse City, Troy, or Grand Rapids, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master’s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men’s and women’s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It’s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state’s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions — Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more — are within easy reach of the city’s central location in Michigan’s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see “Know Your Rights ” posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU’s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education’s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU’s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity?  Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong?  (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in marketing, communications, journalism, public relations, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have at least two years of professional marketing  experience with demonstrated success executing multi-channel marketing efforts? Yes No * Do you have experience developing and managing content across multiple platforms, including social media (LinkedIn, Meta), web, email/CRM systems, blogs, and print/traditional marketing materials? Yes No * Do you have experience working with CRM platforms (e.g., Slate) to support email communications, audience segmentation, and campaign execution? Yes No * Do you have experience collaborating with cross-functional teams and managing projects across multiple stakeholders and priorities? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution.  CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright © Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
