    "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45371": {
      "title": "CMU Applicant Portal | TELECOM SPECIALIST I/II/III",
      "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | TELECOM SPECIALIST I/II/III Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary’s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. TELECOM SPECIALIST I/II/III Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU’s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3956 Position Number 75200 Type of Recruitment External Position Title TELECOM SPECIALIST I/II/III Position Summary Responsible for administrative and technical planning for services provided by CMU sub-divisions Unified Communications, OIT and CONNECT / OIT . Duties include programming of a variety of complex communication and security services and other departmental operations and special projects, as assigned. Duties also include providing a high-level customer service experience to all constituents, maintenance of the billing system database and assisting with the management of CMU student employees. Other key aspects of work at this level include a high degree of independence and latitude to make decisions regarding customer credit, decisions regarding the best service plan for a customer, and decisions regarding work assignment prioritization. Required Qualifications (ST-1) Telecom Specialist I: High school diploma or GED . One year of professional experience. Knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Experience working with customers or in a customer service industry. Experience using spreadsheets. Demonstrated ability to work with discretion. Demonstrated organizational skills with strong attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines with assistance. Demonstrated ability to accurately perform work assignments and construct documents. General knowledge of VoIP telephony. General understanding of standard and multi-line telephone features. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and project a positive attitude. (ST-2) Telecom Specialist II: All of the qualifications of Telecom Specialist I, plus; Three years of related telecommunications experience of a qualifying nature. Experience using databases. Experience coordinating the work of students or interns. Demonstrated ability to independently manage multiple projects and meet deadlines. Thorough knowledge of VoIP telephony. Thorough understanding of standard and multi-line telephone features. (ST-3) Sr. Telecom Specialist: All of the qualifications of Telecom Specialist II, plus; Five years of related telecommunications experience of a qualifying nature. Demonstrated ability to work independently and employ project management skills to organize multiple projects and meet deadlines. Skilled as a solution architect for VoIP telephony. Extensive experience creating complex voicemail trees with scalability. Extensive experience with hunt pilots, call handlers, call routing, and call management. Preferred Qualifications (ST-1) Telecom Specialist I: One year of related telecommunications experience of a qualifying nature. Experience coordinating the work of students or interns. Experience with Microsoft Office Suite, ERP , and updating database information. (ST-2) Telecom Specialist II: Knowledge of ITSM and call accounting software. Experience providing customer training, or generating and presenting solutions to customers. (ST-3) Sr. Telecom Specialist: Project management experience. Solution architect experience. Duties & Responsibilities (ST-1) Telecom Specialist I: Assists customers with cell phone services; verifies accuracy of billing and assists customers with billing issues. Handles requests for service, transfer of service, and loaners for cell phones. Handles customer billing and phone service issues; explains various charges and application of those charges. Generation of service orders and technical support orders for phone and data services. Utilizes ITSM software to track phone order or request status. Utilizes call accounting software to enter customer and billing information. Handles the most basic adds, moves, changes requests for VoIP devices. (ST-2) Telecom Specialist II: All of the duties of Telecom Specialist I plus; Programs VoIP and cellular devices and features using Cisco Unified Communication Manager, or appropriate software. Instructs users on utilization and availability of phone features and options on users phones. Personal voicemail programming. Instructs users on setting up and using voicemail services. Activates and deactivates 800 numbers; sets-up new on-campus and off-campus 800 number accounts. Analyzes bills for video conference room, software and equipment resale, mediated projects, multi-media projects, technical (computer) repair, development services and all other OIT services and coordinates with all these areas of OIT to verify that billings are accurate. Assists customers with issues regarding SAP reconciliation of Telecom/ OIT bills. Analyzes vendor bills and verifies for accuracy. Assists with programming the access control system and video management system, as well as any other safety and security subsystems. Serves as point of contact for service requests. Creates and tracks work requests and works closely with installation technicians to assure timely resolution of service issues. Oversees issuing and assigning access rights for access control and revoking of rights. Investigates requests and troubleshoots problems where appropriate. (ST-3) Sr. Telecom Specialist: All of the duties of Telecom Specialist II plus; Designs/architects solutions for user offices using extensive VoIP feature knowledge combined with understanding/knowledge of user needs and business practices. Responsible for in-depth/complex voicemail call handler programming. Responsible for contact center application programming. Responsible for reconciliation of telephony services to call accounting software utilizing phone database. Provides technical research capability to perform call trace procedures. Attends project meetings pertaining to security integration. Assists on new projects in both existing areas and new construction helping with technology upgrades, product selections and testing. Supports security system integration. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU’s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Supervisory Technical Staff Pay Level Pay Range Starting Rate Between: $16.50 - $26.00 per hour Division President Department Connect - OIT Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as required. Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master’s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men’s and women’s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It’s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state’s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions — Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more — are within easy reach of the city’s central location in Michigan’s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see “Know Your Rights ” posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU’s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education’s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU’s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends 09/08/2026 Open Until Filled No Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong?  (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * How did you first learn of this job opportunity?  Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of professional experience? Yes No * Do you have experience working with customers or in a customer service industry? Yes No * Do you have experience using spreadsheets? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) List of References Certification Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution.  CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright © Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
